2026-11-19 01:49:22 - Agent_20261119014706 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed all four queries for the CVE-2023-23931 class (unvalidated ffi.from_buffer). Confirmed the genuine vulnerability: _CipherContext.update_into in src/cryptography/hazmat/backends/openssl/ciphers.py (lines 157-166) passes the caller-supplied `buf` straight to ffi.from_buffer and then uses it as EVP_CipherUpdate's output pointer with no writability/isinstance check on cryptography 39.0.0 (core version verified). Readonly/bytes buffers are therefore written to by OpenSSL (PyBUF_WRITABLE-style failure / memory corruption), and the two public wrappers _CipherContext.update_into (base.py:178) and _AEADCipherContext.update_into (base.py:219) propagate it without validation. All remaining ~19 locations were verified false positives: they are input-only from_buffer uses (key/nonce/tweak/IV/AAD/tag/password/data fed to read-only parameters), and docstring/error-string literals that merely document the missing check.
