2026-11-19 01:49:43 - Agent_20261119014706 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Both CodeQL results point to `src/_cffi_src/utils.py`, which is a build-time-only helper used by `setup.py` (`src/_cffi_src/build_openssl.py:ffi`) to generate the cffi bindings for the cryptography package. Line 17's `exec(f.read(), about)` reads the package's own shipped `cryptography/__about__.py` from a path derived from `__file__` inside the installed source tree; there is no attacker-controlled input (no evaluation of user data, strings, or network/file input). Line 42's `__import__(module_prefix + name)` is invoked with a hard-coded prefix `"_cffi_src.openssl."` and a static literal module list from `build_openssl.py`, and the imported modules are repo-internal `_cffi_src` modules, not untrusted data. Neither executes during runtime library use — they only run when building from source, at which point an attacker who can modify these files already controls the build. No deserialization of untrusted data and no eval of external input; both reported locations are false positives. No additional vulnerabilities were identified during review.
